PART 0 - EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
==============================================================================


## 0.1 Concept in One Sentence

Element Shift is a 2D puzzle-platformer in which the player controls a single character who instantly transforms between four elemental forms - Fire, Water, Earth, and Wood - each with unique traversal and interaction abilities, to solve environmental puzzles across four progressively harder worlds.


## 0.2 Elevator Pitch

Fireboy & Watergirl proved that elemental abilities create satisfying physical puzzles. Element Shift takes that DNA and compresses it into a single character with an Omnitrix-style instant-swap mechanic, turning every level into a rapid-fire decision tree: "which element, right now?" Short, bite-sized levels (60-180 seconds each) make it an ideal mobile casual title, while optional stars, hidden collectibles, and combo puzzles give it depth for players who want to master it.


## 0.3 Why This Game, Why Now

  - Puzzle-platformers with clear, teachable rules perform consistently well in casual mobile (see Fireboy & Watergirl mobile ports, Two Dots, Heads Up puzzle-platform hybrids).
  - The single-character transformation hook is a differentiator versus the original two-character co-op formula, and removes the friction of needing a second player or AI partner.
  - Flutter + Flame allows a single codebase to ship Android first and iOS/Web later with minimal rework, which matters for a small or solo team.
  - Short session length (2-4 minutes per level) fits mobile play patterns and supports a fair ad-based monetization model without punishing players.


## 0.4 Target Audience

| Segment | Description | Why They Play |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary | Casual puzzle players, ages 10-35, mobile-first | Bite-sized brain teasers, satisfying "aha" moments |
| Secondary | Platformer fans nostalgic for Fireboy & Watergirl-style games | Familiar mechanics, new single-character twist |
| Tertiary | Completionists / speedrunners | Star ratings, hidden collectibles, time trials |


## 0.5 Scope Summary

| Dimension | Target |
| --- | --- |
| Worlds | 4 at launch (Fire, Dual-Element, Timing, Advanced Combination themes) |
| Levels | 60 at launch (15 per world), expandable via updates |
| Playable elements | 4 (Fire, Water, Earth, Wood) - all unlocked progressively across World 1 |
| Session length | 60-180 seconds per level; 20-40 minutes per play session |
| Monetization | Free-to-play, rewarded video ads, optional interstitials, one-time "Remove Ads + Bonus Skins" IAP |
| Engine | Flutter + Flame Engine (Dart) |
| Target build size | < 150 MB initial download (Android App Bundle) |


## 0.6 Success Criteria

  1. Prototype proves the transformation feel (< 0.3s swap, readable silhouette change) is fun in under 10 test levels.
  2. Vertical slice (World 1, 15 levels) achieves an average external playtester completion rate above 80% without hints.
  3. Beta build maintains 55+ FPS on a mid-tier Android device (e.g., 3-year-old mid-range phone) across all worlds.
  4. Day-1 to Day-7 retention benchmarks are met or exceeded relative to genre comparables before wide marketing spend.
  5. Monetization does not require an interstitial or rewarded ad to complete any level - ads are always optional value-adds.



