### 17.2 Event Bus (Flutter ↔ Flame boundary)

A small set of typed, one-directional events crosses the Flutter/Flame boundary. This is intentionally a short, closed list — new cross-boundary needs should extend this table, not create ad-hoc callbacks.

| Direction | Event/Command | Payload | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Flame → Flutter | LevelCompleted | levelId, stars, shardsCollected, timeElapsed, swapCount | Trigger SaveService write, show completion UI, evaluate rewarded-ad prompts |
| Flame → Flutter | CheckpointReached | levelId, checkpointIndex | Optional analytics event |
| Flame → Flutter | RewardedAdRequested | context (hint/doubleShards) | Flutter invokes AdsService, then calls back into Flame with result |
| Flutter → Flame | LoadLevel | levelId | Instructs LevelLoader to build a new LevelWorld |
| Flutter → Flame | ApplySettings | controlScheme, hudScale, hapticEnabled, audioLevels | Pushes live settings changes into the running game |
| Flutter → Flame | GrantHint / GrantDoubleShards | - | Result of a completed rewarded ad watch |


## 18. Save System


### 18.1 Data to Persist

| Data | Structure | Storage Choice |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Level results | Map<levelId, {stars, bestTimeMs, minSwaps, shardsCollected}> | Structured local DB (Hive/sqflite) |
| World unlock state | Derived from level results at read time (not separately stored) to avoid sync bugs | Computed, not stored |
| Economy | elementShardBalance (int), ownedSkins (Set<SkinId>) | Structured local DB |
| Settings | controlScheme, hudScale, audioLevels, hapticEnabled, colorblindIconMode | shared_preferences (simple key-values) |
| Ad/IAP state | adsRemoved (bool), lastInterstitialShownAt (timestamp) | shared_preferences |


### 18.2 Save Architecture

A single `SaveService` (Flutter-layer, injected via Riverpod) is the only component permitted to read/write persistent storage. Flame-layer systems never touch storage directly — they emit events (see §17.2) that the Flutter layer translates into SaveService calls. This keeps the Flame layer portable and testable without a storage backend.

```
PlayerComponent / ObjectiveSystem
        │  LevelCompleted(levelId, stars, time, swaps, shards)
        ▼
   AppStateController (Flutter)
        │
        ▼
    SaveService.recordLevelResult(...)
        │
        ▼
  Local DB (Hive box: 'progress')  ──periodic──▶  (optional) cloud backup
                                                   via platform save (Play Games /
                                                   iCloud) — stretch goal
```


### 18.3 Save Timing & Integrity Rules

  - Write on every LevelCompleted event immediately — never batch level results, since losing a completion is the worst-case failure for this genre.
  - Settings and economy changes are debounced (e.g., 500ms) to avoid excessive disk writes during rapid UI interaction (like dragging a volume slider).
  - Star/best-time records are only ever improved, never overwritten downward — SaveService.recordLevelResult must merge with max(stars), min(bestTimeMs).
  - A schema version field is stored alongside save data from day one, so future updates can run migrations instead of resetting progress.


### 18.4 Cloud Save (Stretch Goal)

Post-launch, local saves can be mirrored to Google Play Games Services (Android) and Game Center (iOS) save state APIs, keyed by the same schema-versioned structure, to support device transfer without requiring a custom backend.


