PART VII — FUTURE EXPANSION IDEAS
==============================================================================

Ideas intentionally out of scope for the initial 60-level, 4-world launch, listed here so they are captured without inflating launch scope.


## 35. Content Expansions

  - World 5+: a fifth element (e.g., Air/Wind or Ice as a distinct form rather than an environmental state) introduced via a content update.
  - Daily rotating Challenge Levels reusing existing tilesets with new hazard/switch layouts (§9.4) — low art cost, high replay value.
  - Seasonal/limited-time cosmetic skins tied to real-world events, sold only for Element Shards (never real money) to preserve fairness.
  - A level editor / community levels mode, gated behind a moderation or curation system if enabled.


## 36. Systems Expansions

  - Cloud save via Play Games Services / Game Center (§18.4).
  - Leaderboards and friend challenges for par-time and minimum-swap records (§9.4).
  - Expanded Codex/lore system with unlockable world-building content (teased as a stretch goal in §7.3/§9.3).
  - Additional accessibility options: full button remapping presets, colorblind palette variants beyond the shape-coding already in scope.
  - Analytics-driven dynamic difficulty suggestions (e.g., surfacing the hint ad slightly earlier for players who fail a level many times), always opt-in.


## 37. Platform Expansions

  - iOS release following Android launch, reusing the same Flutter/Flame codebase with platform-specific IAP/ad SDK wiring.
  - Web build (Flutter Web) as a promotional/demo version, likely capped to World 1 content for a fast-loading marketing experience.
  - Controller support for potential future desktop/console exploration, made easier by the existing input-abstraction layer (§15.1 PlayerInputComponent).
